    "proved": [
      "Complete shared complex-shape scalar system retains both determinant and parallel components, phases, edge transformations and all total Z/C contributions.",
      "A linear receiver in a cancelling row forces each area-nonzero sender across a beta-zero edge to have strictly larger frequency length. Mixed linear/area-nonzero types force complete W0 nonzero.",
      "For any independent integer longest receiver and exactly two active linear senders, the full zero mixed row forces the receiver to be linear. No reverse-beta constraint or sender-sender nonorthogonality is needed for this row lemma.",
      "In the original nonorthogonal distinct-length active triangle, exactly two linear seeds cannot satisfy total M0=0. Every fixed datum in that branch has complete m=norm(M0)>0 and w=norm(W0)>0.",
      "The accepted same-datum NS bridge gives an explicit local window with m/(3w)<=norm(R)/norm(S)<=3m/w and limit m/w>0. This excludes achieving zero limiting source ratio solely by shrinking time for that datum."
